RPrint


A  port of the RPrint program for any Amiga with WB2.0+. This software
is public domain.


RPrint  is an equivalent utility to that which came with the PC Psion
link  cable for IBM compatibles, it prints using the computer to copy
the serial output from the Psion to the printer.



Installing RPrint.

Go  to  or  make  a  directory  where RPrint will live. Put disk with
RPrint in any drive, and double click on disks icon. Select 'Show all
files'  from  WB  screen menu. Go into the RPrint directory. Drag the
RPrint  icon  into the drawer where it is to live. Drag the icon that
looks  best  into the drawer as well (only drag one icon). Select the
icon  you have just dragged, then choose 'Rename' from the icon menu.
Rename  the  icon  as  'RPrint'. The installation on the Amiga is now
finished.

On  the  Psion  press  the system button. Go to the control menu, and
select  'Printer'.  Set Printer Device to 'Serial'. Set the following
device characteristics:

    Baud rate: 19200 for a Series 3a, 9600 for a Series3

    Data bits: 8

    Stop bits: 1

    Parity: None

    Ignoreparity: No

Set the following Serial handshaking:

    Xon/Xoff: Off

    Rts/Cts: On

    Dsr/Dtr: Off

    Dcd: Off

If  you set the baud rate to 9600, you now must go back to the Amiga.
Select  the  RPrint  Icon, and select the Information option from the
icon menu. Change the BaudRate Tool Type to 9600.

You  may  now  print to the printer connected to your Amiga using the
Series 3.



Advanced Usage.

    The program is controlled by several tool types. These are:

·  'Baudrate' this sets the speed of transfer.

·  'Timeout' this is the timein seconds it takes after the last piece
of  data  has been transmitted for the program to assume printing has
ceased. 

·  'Device'  sets  the  serial device used. (Change this if you have a
serial card with the Psion attached)

·  'Unit'  sets  the unit on the serial device. (Change if you have a
multi serial card) 

·  'Output'  where the output from the Psion should go. This can be a
file,  such  as  'Work:PsionPrint.prt'.  Thus  RPrint  may be used to
transfer   files  using  the  comms  application  on  ASCII  transfer
protocol.   

This  program  was  written in Blitz Basic II (which accounts for its
large size!) by Tim Chick.

